<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="024" project="spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>E2 eval cases — dead-end suppression + card gating (FR-10)</title>
    <phase>2 — E2 follow-ons</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>TEST-MODIFYING — adds eval/test coverage; per CLAUDE.md the test-modifying override makes code-review + adr-check unconditional at Step 9.5.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Adds eval/unit cases against already-specified FR-04 / FR-06 behaviors; test authoring following the ADR-039 golden-utterance + ADR-038 obligations — no architectural judgment.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>Wave2-E2</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Adds eval/test files only — no shared production-file rewrite; still /conflict-check before the PR.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>021, 023</deps>
    <tags>testing, eval</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>
  <prompt>Add E2 eval/unit cases so FR-04 (no dead-end follow-on) and FR-06 (card gating) are covered and FAIL on regression. Cases: (1) an unbacked free-string suggestion does NOT render; (2) "prioritize my tasks" either works (maps to the FR-01 advisory capability) or is absent; (3) the Daily Briefing / Smart To Do follow-on cards are gated on the tab's open state (suppressed when open, shown+launch when closed). A reintroduced dead-end suggestion or an ungated card MUST fail these cases (negative). Follow the ADR-039 golden-utterance suite + the ADR-038 eval-case obligation.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE developer with eval/test expertise. Comfortable with the ADR-039 golden-utterance eval suite, the ADR-038 integration-heavy testing strategy + eval-case obligation, and the SprkChat / ConversationPane follow-on subsystems being covered.</role>
  <goal>FR-04 (no dead-end follow-on) and FR-06 (card gating) are covered by eval/unit cases that pass now and fail if the behavior regresses — a reintroduced dead-end suggestion or an ungated card fails them.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-10 — the eval-case guardrail: every new/changed AI behavior lands with an eval case (ADR-039 golden-utterance suite + maker-guide obligation, ADR-038). This task adds the E2 coverage for the two behaviors shipped by tasks 021 (suggestion gating) and 023 (follow-on card gating). Case set: (1) an unbacked free-string `SprkChatSuggestions` entry is suppressed / not rendered (guards FR-04 / task 021); (2) "prioritize my tasks" maps to the FR-01 advisory capability and works, or does not render (guards FR-04); (3) the Daily Briefing and Smart To Do follow-on cards render only when the target tab is closed and are suppressed when it is open (guards FR-06 / task 023). Each case MUST be a genuine regression guard — a re-introduced dead-end or an ungated card fails it. Deps: 021 (the suggestion gate) + 023 (the gated cards) must land first so there is behavior to cover.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>the ADR-039 golden-utterance eval suite (add the FR-04 / FR-06 cases here)</file>
      <file>the SprkChat suggestion gate unit test suite (task 021 output — extend for the unbacked-suppression + "prioritize my tasks" cases)</file>
      <file>the ConversationPane follow-on-card tests (task 023 output — extend for the open/closed card-gating cases)</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r4/spec.md (FR-04 / FR-06 / FR-10 acceptance)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-038" scope="the eval/unit cases">Follow the integration-heavy testing strategy + eval-case obligation; each case is a real regression guard (fails on reintroduced dead-end / ungated card), not a scaffolding/DI-registration/ctor-null test.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-039" scope="the eval cases">Add cases to the golden-utterance suite covering the advisory-capability behaviors (FR-01-backed "prioritize my tasks") without adding a classifier / second decider under test.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project" scope="coverage">Cover BOTH FR-04 (no dead-end follow-on) and FR-06 (card gating) with negative cases that fail on regression (§NFR-08 test obligation).</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r4/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r4/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Add an eval/unit case: an unbacked free-string suggestion does NOT render (guards FR-04 / task 021).</step>
    <step order="2">Add a case: "prioritize my tasks" maps to the FR-01 advisory capability and works, or is absent (guards FR-04).</step>
    <step order="3">Add cases: the Daily Briefing / Smart To Do follow-on cards are gated on the tab's open state — suppressed when open, shown + launching the correct surface when closed (guards FR-06 / task 023).</step>
    <step order="4">Confirm each case passes on current behavior and fails when the guarded behavior is regressed (reintroduced dead-end / ungated card).</step>
    <step order="5">/conflict-check before the PR; update TASK-INDEX ✅.</step>
  </steps>
  <justification>
    <existing>The ADR-039 golden-utterance suite + the task-021/023 test suites exist; no E2 dead-end / card-gating coverage exists yet.</existing>
    <extension>Add cases to the existing suites — no new test harness.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>FR-04 / FR-06 can regress silently: a dead-end suggestion or an ungated (duplicate-tab) card could reappear with no failing test.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
  <outputs>
    <output type="test">FR-04 eval/unit cases (unbacked suggestion suppressed; "prioritize my tasks" works or absent)</output>
    <output type="test">FR-06 eval/unit cases (Briefing / Smart To Do cards gated on tab open state)</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The FR-04 cases are added and pass (unbacked suggestion does not render; "prioritize my tasks" works or is absent).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The FR-06 cases are added and pass (Briefing / Smart To Do cards suppressed when the tab is open, shown when closed).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A reintroduced dead-end suggestion fails the FR-04 case (negative).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An ungated card (that would open a duplicate tab) fails the FR-06 case (negative).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>Deps 021 + 023 must land first (behavior to cover). Cover both FR-04 and FR-06 with genuine negative regression guards per ADR-038 (no scaffolding/DI/ctor-null tests). Add "prioritize my tasks" to the ADR-039 golden-utterance suite as an FR-01-backed case. /conflict-check before the PR.</notes>
  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting, load all files in knowledge/files. Follow task-execute skill.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
